    "explanation": "1. PRIMARY (PROJECTION_MINIFICATION): The 4K panorama (W=4096 across 360\u00b0) has an angular resolution of 11.38 px/deg, whereas the physical S23 camera stills have 51.69 px/deg (f=2961.7 px). This represents a mandatory 4.54x linear minification (~20.6 source pixels compressed into 1 panorama pixel). Point-sampling this footprint with simple bilinear interpolation drops high-frequency details. At 12K (W=12288), resolution increases to 34.13 px/deg, reducing minification to only 1.51x.\n2. SECONDARY (VIEWER_GPU_FILTERING): The viewer code contained a selector omission in resolveAndLoadTexture() which caused it to load the old AI reference panorama JPEG (P2R16_AI_QUALITY12_OWNER_REVIEW.jpg) instead of P2R16_R4P83_SELECTED_4K.png, displaying a 4096x608 HUD label, an old compressed JPEG texture, and a 161\u00b0 rotated yaw frame.\n3. TERTIARY (BILINEAR_FILTER_LOSS): Sampling without a sinc/Lanczos or area pre-filtering kernel slightly smooths high-contrast edge slopes."
